  "question": {
    "text": "$n$ - digit numbers are formed using only three digits 2,5 and 7 . The smallest value of $n$ for which 900 such distinct numbers can be formed, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n6\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n 8\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n9\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n7",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Required $n$ digit numbers is $3^n$ as each place can be filled by $2,5,7$.\nSo smallest value of $n$ such that $3^n>900$. Therefore $n=7$."
  }
}